  message: "FIXED ON A LOCAL BRANCH, NOT INTEGRATED (2026-10-04). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/lopus (worktree ~/hg_wt/lopus), based on the stage-8 integration branch 2a98abb55d. Commits: f9052cbde3 (rust), b0a42e613d (docs + pin). Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/lopus.md.\n\nWHAT: rust.py emits a `function` symbol for every function_signature_item directly inside a foreign_mod_item, with meta[\"ffi_import\"] = the binding the source states (abi, \"C\" when unwritten; wasm_bindgen js_namespace / js_name -> foreign_name / module -> js_module; #[link(name)] -> link; #[link_name] -> foreign_name). Registered in axis_meta_keys, docs/schema.json regenerated, spec key count 54 -> 55. rust_scip parity holds (it already recomputed a stable id for an unowned signature item).\n\nSECOND MANIFESTATION (mod helpers { fn now } + use helpers::*): a bare call now prefers the free function the CALLER's module declares, so the root-level now() binds to the extern declaration and a now() inside mod helpers binds to helpers::now (both pinned).\n\nA REGRESSION THE FIRST A/B CAUGHT AND THE BRANCH CLOSES: the new symbol was the one `now` in loro, and the method / Type:: fallback bound all 44 Instant::now() / SystemTime::now() chains to it. A foreign declaration is now reachable only by its bare name or the module path it is declared under (kept out of the method pool; Strategy 2 does not bind a path or receiver call to it; cross-file it does not capture a name the file use-binds outside the crate). The same three doors stay open for ordinary in-repo free functions: filed as WI-hilib-hutor-sifab-busat-tipud-vabah-nilid-bunob.\n\nEVIDENCE: io-boundaries A/B by chain, arm A = exported 2a98abb55d, arm B = branch, fresh XDG caches, --include-tests. loro 5483 -> 5482: the one removed chain is host_info_read std::time::Instant.now <- crates/loro-internal/src/change.rs:300-311 get_sys_timestamp (the filed site); 0 added. pdfium-render 1332 -> 1332 (its bindgen files are not analysed, and its blocks are Rust 2024 `unsafe extern`). Item repro (extern \"C\" { fn now(); fn getpid(); } + callers): io-boundaries reports no chain; native -> rust:src/lib.rs:1-1:now:function, resolved.\n\nNOT DONE / FILED: unsafe extern blocks do not parse in tree-sitter-rust 0.24.0 (WI-kipun-naral-nuhin-bozir-kinud-gafug-lulav-mafoz); a call to a foreign declaration is classified by NO catalogue, so loro's Date.now clock read is now unreported (WI-fomab-sozir-jovot-boduh-mutad-nuhah-gadab-laram, the foreign-catalogue redirect)."  # 96f0
